{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/php/php-src/issues/24792","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/php/php-src","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/php/php-src/issues/24792/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/php/php-src/issues/24792/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/php/php-src/issues/24792/events","html_url":"https://github.com/php/php-src/issues/24792","id":6062476605,"node_id":"I_kwDOAB0Los8AAAABaVoNPQ","number":24792,"title":"PHP 8.6: Assignment-result writes compile but fail with invalid opcode","user":{"login":"alwyn1024","id":2869280,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI4NjkyODA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2869280?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alwyn1024","html_url":"https://github.com/alwyn1024","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alwyn1024/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alwyn1024/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alwyn1024/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alwyn1024/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alwyn1024/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alwyn1024/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alwyn1024/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alwyn1024/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alwyn1024/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":148912283,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxNDg5MTIyODM=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/php/php-src/labels/Bug","name":"Bug","color":"E99695","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":3611416941,"node_id":"LA_kwDOAB0Los7XQdlt","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/php/php-src/labels/Status:%20Needs%20Triage","name":"Status: Needs Triage","color":"D93F0B","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":1,"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:36:30Z","updated_at":"2026-11-06T07:51:53Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Description\n\n## Summary\n\nIn PHP 8.6.0RC4, writing to an array dimension on an assignment result compiles successfully, but execution fails with an `Invalid opcode` fatal error.\n\nPHP 8.5.10 rejects the same construct during compilation.\n\n## Minimal reproducer\n\n```php\n<?php\n($a = [1])[0] = 2;\nvar_dump($a);\n```\n\n### Actual behavior\n\n**PHP 8.5.10:** Compilation fails:\n\n```\nFatal error: Cannot use temporary expression in write context\n```\n\n**PHP 8.6.0RC4:** `php -l` succeeds, but executing the code fails:\n\n```\nFatal error: Invalid opcode 23/2/1.\n```\n\n### Reference-assignment control\n\n```php\n<?php\n$b = [1];\n($a =& $b)[0] = 2;\nvar_dump($a, $b);\n```\n\nPHP 8.6.0RC4 accepts and executes this successfully, with both arrays containing `[2]`.\n\nOther assignment-derived property writes, destructuring-result writes, compound assignments, `unset`, and reference-binding operations exhibit related discrepancies.\n\n## Expected behavior / clarification requested\n\nShould assignment-derived dimension and property writes be rejected during compilation, or should PHP generate valid writable operands for these expressions?\n\nIn particular, is the ordinary-assignment failure a compiler emission defect, a missing compile-time rejection, or an intentional distinction between ordinary and reference-assignment results?\n\n## Affected versions\n\n- PHP 8.5.10 — Windows x64\n- PHP 8.6.0RC4 — Windows x64, NTS, VC2022\n- PHP 8.6 source commit: `f23b4c222cebe33be93ee8ecaaa14390c5507a08`\n\nThe PHP 8.6 executable was built from the specified source commit.\n\nReproduction: `php -n -l example.php`, followed by `php -n example.php`.\n\n## Relevant implementation\n\n- [[zend_compile_var_inner](https://github.com/php/php-src/blob/f23b4c222cebe33be93ee8ecaaa14390c5507a08/Zend/zend_compile.c#L12774)](https://github.com/php/php-src/blob/f23b4c222cebe33be93ee8ecaaa14390c5507a08/Zend/zend_compile.c#L12774)\n- [[ZEND_ASSIGN_DIM handlers](https://github.com/php/php-src/blob/f23b4c222cebe33be93ee8ecaaa14390c5507a08/Zend/zend_vm_def.h#L2680)](https://github.com/php/php-src/blob/f23b4c222cebe33be93ee8ecaaa14390c5507a08/Zend/zend_vm_def.h#L2680)\n- [[Related PR #20628](https://github.com/php/php-src/pull/20628)](https://github.com/php/php-src/pull/20628)\n\nThe compiler appears to allow assignment ASTs in writable contexts while producing operand kinds unsupported by the corresponding VM write handlers.\n\nI would appreciate clarification of the intended behavior before treating these forms as valid or invalid PHP source syntax.\n\n### PHP Version\n\n```plain\nPHP 8.6.0RC4 (cli) (built: Oct 25 2026 12:45:36) (NTS Visual C++ 2022 x64)\nCopyright © The PHP Group and Contributors\nZend Engine v4.6.0RC4, Copyright © Zend by Perforce\n    with Zend OPcache v8.6.0RC4, Copyright ©, by Zend by Perforce\n```\n\n### Operating System\n\nWindows x64 (64-bit), PHP 8.6.0RC4 NTS, Visual C++ 2022 (VC17)","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/php/php-src/issues/24792/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/php/php-src/issues/24792/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}